Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.4.14
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. Stage 1 applies a configurable
    min_cells threshold before normalization, with a default of 500, and passes
    the same retained cell set to downstream metacell construction. Stage 2 uses
    a configurable min_cells_per_stratum threshold that also defaults to 500.
    Routing is resolved independently for every broad cell type. A cell type
    with at least two retained conditions uses Pando's native condition-GRN
    procedure. Candidate edges are discovered on the complete cell type and
    separately in every retained condition, and exact TF-peak-target triples are
    unioned into a broad candidate dictionary. A preliminary joint multi-task
    ridge fit supplies condition-wise ridge-Wald P values; BH-adjusted significant
    edges are unioned across conditions to form the actual shared fit dictionary.
    The default adjusted-P threshold is 0.05 and condition analysis permits a
    configured threshold up to 0.1. All conditions for each target are then
    refitted jointly on that same significant-union dictionary with ridge
    regression and a symmetric fusion penalty. Predictor regularization uses one
    equal-condition within-condition RMS scale, one target-specific lambda shared
    across conditions is selected by condition-stratified cross-validation, and
    exported coefficients are back-transformed to raw TF-by-ATAC units. In the
    final refit, a condition-specific coefficient contributes to RegCompass only
    when it is estimable, belongs to an ok target fit, and its BH-adjusted
    ridge-Wald P value is below the configured threshold. Pairwise direct
    condition contrasts beta_A-beta_B are retained separately from condition-wise
    edge significance. Condition-specific zero-variance edges can remain in the
    common fit dictionary when supported in another condition but contribute zero
    in a condition where they are not estimable. A cell type with one retained
    condition uses the original standard Pando GRN and creates no condition
    coefficient. Standard Pando uses the configured fixed tf_cor and peak_cor
    candidate thresholds without cell-count-dependent adjustment. RegCompass
    owns the outer parallel scheduler. Condition-mode Pando objects are
    initialized independently by broad cell type. When several cell types are
    present they are run as independent outer jobs with nested target parallelism
    disabled; when one condition-mode cell type is present the same worker budget
    can be used by Pando across target-level multi-task fits. Different cell
    types retain their own Pando objects and local peak/motif feature spaces.
    Standard Pando is parallelized only across independent broad cell types. For
    RegCompass Layer 1, TF and ATAC values are separately averaged over exact
    SuperCell membership before regulatory multiplication, preserving beta times
    mean(TF) times mean(ATAC) as the condition regulatory projection. Metacells
    use one multimodal WNN graph per broad cell type and remain condition-pure
    after membership splitting. Optional raw ATAC fragment files are aggregated
    to final metacell barcodes and recounted before metacell TF-IDF. Quantitative
    RNA for the LP penalty is normalized on the linear CPM scale per original
    cell and then averaged with equal cell weight inside exact final SuperCell
    membership; aggregated-count latent CPM remains restricted to bounded
    structural confidence. RNA support, regulatory effects, GPR rules,
    cell-type-specific union GEM construction and directional penalties use
    consistent reaction ordering, bounds and medium scenarios. Stage 5 uses the
    original MATLAB CORDA2 algorithm from
    schultzdre/Constraint-Based-Modeling/CORDA2.m as the default context-specific
    completion after mapping cell-type multiome evidence to HC, MC, NC and OT
    reactions. FASTCORE and complete full-GEM scoring remain explicit
    supplementary routes. The adjustable original controls are MCxNCthresh,
    constraint, constrainby, om and ci under corda2_args. Actively reversible
    reactions are split once, the opposite directional copy is closed during
    each target assessment, and the original Step 1, Step 2.1, Step 2.2 and Step
    3 dependency transitions are preserved. With parallel Layer 2 execution,
    directional targets are parallelized only within the current CORDA2 step,
    all results are reduced in original directional order at a strict step
    barrier, and the step-local worker pool is released before the next step
    begins. Cell-type-by-medium models remain independent and are reused by
    primary and RNA-only scoring.
